      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The existence of massive financial flows from the fossil fuel industry into politicians' pockets has effectively corrupted the democratic process, rendering policy decisions a mere puppet show for corporate interests. In a system where money talks louder than votes, the voices of ordinary citizens are drowned out, and the interests of the wealthy and powerful are prioritized over those of the general population. It's not just a matter of \"who has the most lobbyist money,\" but rather, the entire system is rigged to favor those who can afford to buy influence, effectively disenfranchising the majority of the population.",
      "source": "target",
